    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with significant firepower at the top of the lineup, led by our two highest-projected options: **Yordan Alvarez** (82.19) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13). **Yordan Alvarez** offers the highest floor and ceiling, benefiting from an elite xwOBA of 0.473 against a favorable 4.48 xERA matchup. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our primary engine for stolen bases; while his matchup against Lugo includes a slight penalty for the pitcher's elite pickoff/hold ability, his premier spot at the top of the order and positive park factors make him a mandatory start. **Trea Turner** (79.76) and **Kyle Schwarber** (78.41) also present elite scoring opportunities today, both drawing favorable matchups against the vulnerable 5.31 xERA of Scherzer, with **Trea Turner** receiving a key boost from the pitcher's slow delivery, which remains our primary indicator for aggressive baserunning opportunities.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Jacob Gonzalez** (35.99) and **Chase Meidroth** (34.97), both of whom fell well short of our 40-point efficiency floor. **Jacob Gonzalez** was the closest to contention, but his score was severely hampered by a daunting 3.43 xERA matchup against Stock and a negative park factor, forcing him to the pine to preserve our daily game caps. While **Christian Yelich** (59.83) and **Caleb Durbin** (65.55) anchor the back end of our active roster, we remain wary of the platoon-heavy nature of today's lineup. **Dillon Dingler** (44.01) sits on the lower end of our active scorers due to a significant platoon disadvantage against Roupp, but his presence in the heart of the order and favorable wind conditions keep him just above the bench threshold. We are monitoring **Kazuma Okamoto** and **Hector Rodriguez**, but with both currently out of their respective team lineups, there is no viable path for them to contribute to today\u2019s category accumulation.",
